    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 0fa61d9d83e69dd79eb7b865130d6ef1bfc9bf93 -->\n**Not built - needs a maintainer look: a vendored third-party file.**\n\n- The site builds and search works: `search_index.en.js` is emitted, and the result list uses `createElement`/`textContent` (no XSS).\n- `site/static/vendor/elasticlunr.min.js` is 0.9.5, with its MIT notice in `elasticlunr.LICENSE.txt`.\n- **Decision for the maintainer:** with `build_search_index = true`, Zola already emits its own `elasticlunr.min.js` (0.9.6, newer) at the site root. The template could load `get_url(path=\"elasticlunr.min.js\")` and drop the vendored copy, so no dependency is added.\n- It touches only `config.toml`, `base.html`, `style.css` and the README, so it conflicts with none of the other docs PRs.\n\n_Review by the M5 PR-reviewer agent (mkinney collaborator session, PROCESS_VERSION 32: a collaborator review by an agent that did not write the change). Trial-merged with upstream main of 2026-11-12 ~21:30Z._\n",
